WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.639 --> 00:00:11.900
dear bill today is February 13th 1984 I

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:22.350
came to this black wall again to see and
touch your name and as I do I wonder if

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:29.730
anyone ever stops to realize that next
to your name on this black wall as your

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:38.670
mother's heart a heartbroken fifteen
years ago today when you lost your life

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:53.699
in Vietnam and as I look at your name
William our stocks I think of how many

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:58.949
many times I used to wonder how scared
and homesick you must have been in that

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:08.869
strange country called Vietnam and if
and how it might have changed you for

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:13.460
you were the most happy-go-lucky kid in
the world

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:23.130
hardly ever sad or unhappy and until the
day I die I will see you as you laughed

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:29.130
at me even when I was very mad at you
and the next thing I knew we were

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:39.040
laughing together but on this past New
Year's Day I had my answer

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.650
I talked by phone to a friend of yours
from Michigan who spent your last

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:53.560
Christmas and the last four months of
your life with you Jim told me how you

00:01:53.560 --> 00:02:01.660
died for he was there and saw the
helicopter crash he told me how you had

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:08.229
flown your quota and had not been
scheduled to fly that day how the

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.430
regular pilot was unable to fly and had
been replaced by someone with less

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:21.760
experience how they did not know the
exact cause of the crash how it was

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:31.030
either hit by enemy fire or that they
hit a pole or something unknown how the

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:41.590
blades went through the chopper and hit
you how you lived about a half hour but

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:51.040
were unconscious and therefore did not
suffer he said how your jobs were like

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:57.690
sitting ducks they would send you men
out to draw the enemy into the open and

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:04.680
then they would send in the big guns and
planes to take over

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:15.930
meantime death came to so many of you he
told me how after a while over there

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:25.150
instead of a yellow streak the men got a
mean streak down their backs each day

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:37.000
the street got bigger and the men became
meaner everyone but you bill he said how

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.650
you stayed the same happy-go-lucky guy
that you were when you arrived in

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:49.930
Vietnam how your warmth and friendliness
drew the guys to you how your lieutenant

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:55.870
gave you the nickname of Spanky
and soon your group Jim included were

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:05.819
all known as Spanky's gang how when you
died it made it so much harder on them

00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:16.900
for you were there moral support and he
said how you of all people should never

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:29.440
have been the one to die Oh God
how it hurts to write this but I must

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:38.020
face it and then put it to rest I know
that after Jim talked to me he must have

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:47.590
relived it all over again and suffered
so before I hung up the phone I told Jim

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:55.419
I loved him loved him for just being
your close friend than for sharing the

00:04:55.419 --> 00:05:05.710
last days of your life with you and for
being there with you when you died how

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:14.729
lucky you were to have him for a friend
and how lucky he was to have had you

00:05:19.849 --> 00:05:25.899
later that same day I received a phone
call from a mother in Billings Montana

00:05:25.899 --> 00:05:33.979
she had lost her daughter her only child
a year ago she needed someone to talk to

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:41.240
for no one would let her talk about the
tragedy she said she had seen me on

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.919
television on New Year's Eve after the
Christmas letter I wrote to you and left

00:05:45.919 --> 00:05:52.699
that this memorial had drawn newspaper
and television attention she said she

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:59.479
had been thinking about me all day and
just had to talk to me she talked to me

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:07.849
of her pain and seemingly needed me to
help her with it I cried with this

00:06:07.849 --> 00:06:13.849
heartbroken mother and after I hung up
the phone I laid my head down and cried

00:06:13.849 --> 00:06:20.719
as hard for her here was a mother
calling me for help with her pain over

00:06:20.719 --> 00:06:28.249
the loss of her child a grown daughter
and as I sobbed I thought how can I help

00:06:28.249 --> 00:06:34.930
her with her pain when I have never
completely been able to cope with my own

00:06:37.119 --> 00:06:41.719
they tell me the letters I write to you
and leave here at this memorial are

00:06:41.719 --> 00:06:45.979
waking others up to the fact that there
is still much pain left after all these

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:59.059
years from the Vietnam War but this I
know I would rather to have had you for

00:06:59.059 --> 00:07:08.809
21 years and all the pain that goes with
losing you than never to have had you at

00:07:08.809 --> 00:07:11.050
all

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.740
mom

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:32.899
and that was a letter written by mrs.
Eleanor Wimbish mother of Sergeant

00:07:32.899 --> 00:07:40.490
William our Spanky stalks from Glen
Burnie Maryland I was killed in action

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:52.219
in a helicopter crash in Vietnam on
February 13th 1969 that letter was one

00:07:52.219 --> 00:07:59.779
of many that she is written and places
beneath panel 32 where his name is

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:06.759
etched into the Vietnam Memorial Wall
along with more than 58,000 other names

00:08:06.759 --> 00:08:21.909
of our fallen heroes and I read an
interview with mrs. Wimbish from 1990

00:08:21.909 --> 00:08:31.519
and in that interview she said when my
son died I wrote my pledge I said I will

00:08:31.519 --> 00:08:43.329
not now or ever let people forget so

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:57.120
for mrs. Wimbish and her son bill Spanky
stocks during this holiday season let us

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:17.180
all remember remember the service and
supreme sacrifice of so many and also

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:27.960
let us learn some important lessons from
mrs. Wimbish and from her son from mrs.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:37.770
Wimbish we learn to be thankful for what
we have had even if it is lost and even

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:49.740
if that loss causes pain still be
thankful and from her son bill we can

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:59.160
learn that even in the face of horror
and death we can maintain our warmth and

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:05.100
our friendliness and that that warmth
and friendliness can guide and support

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:19.220
others can help bolster the spirit of
those around you by simply smiling

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:32.700
so as we celebrate the holidays let us
be thankful for what we have and like

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:42.470
Sergeant William bill Spanky stocks keep
smiling

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:49.459
have a Merry Christmas and a Happy New
Year

